 "description": "BIGVILLE R3 (block 251000) -- the AUTONOMOUS SLEEP decision + exhaustion COLLAPSE, as graph rules over the R1 energy budget. `bt_decide_sleep` is THE sleep-or-defer decision: a decision_value trade-off (the SAME Argmax/compare family as ss_choose_burn / nd_choose_good) -- a SAFE, LATE agent elects to sleep iff sleep_drive = max(0,sleep_threshold-energy) + safe_bonus*safe + late_bonus*lateness EXCEEDS its goal_urgency (a BUSY agent with a high-urgency unfinished goal DEFERS); ablation `sleep_enabled=0` removes the option so the agent CANNOT sleep and runs to collapse. `bt_collapse` is the involuntary past-threshold collapse (energy<e_collapse while awake) WHEREVER the agent is. `bt_replenish` refills while asleep, gain+cap gated by `collapsed` so collapse sleep is NON-restorative (collapse_cap<rest_cap => the spiral, the temporal twin of the 242000 window-breach). `bt_wake` wakes at the applicable cap (collapsed agents still wake -- non-restorative != permanent). Composes existing Terms (IfThenElse/Max/Minus/Plus/Times/Gt/Gte/Lt/Eq/And) -- zero new Rust. lateness/safe/goal_urgency are world facts the adapter writes mechanically (like hunger); the DECISION is here, never in Python.",
